# ASCII vs accents

This file is the only accent policy. Do not repeat it in other rules.

## Default (program, docs)

- No accents or non-ASCII in the program: new code, comments, logs, docs,
  `how_it_works.md`, terminal output.
- No emojis.
- Reason: PowerShell/Windows (`charmap`) fails on non-ASCII.
- Existing Maya strings may already contain Spanish. Leave them until asked.

## Required exception: chat with the user

Cursor chat replies are Spanish with correct accents. See `chat-language.mdc`.
This exception is only for the message shown to the user. It does not apply
to code, docs, logs, or `how_it_works.md`.

## Summary

| Scope | Accents / non-ASCII |
|---|---|
| Chat with the user (Spanish) | YES, required |
| New code, comments, logs, docs | NO |
| Existing Maya UI strings | leave until asked |
